---
description: ez- component catalog usage — apply when writing prototype templates
globs: prototypes/**/*.vue,blueprint/patterns/**/*.vue
alwaysApply: false
---

The component catalog is `blueprint/ez/CATALOG.md` (when to use what, then the generated API). Read it before writing a template. Components are registered globally: use `<ez-btn>` etc. without importing them. `proto check` rejects unknown components, props and values.

Two tiers: primitives (`ez-btn`, `ez-badge`…, generic) and domain components (`ez-badge-folder-state`…, one business object, built from primitives). Prefer an existing domain component, then primitives assembled.

Page skeleton, always:
```vue
<ez-page>
   <ez-page-header :title="…" />
   <ez-page-content>
      …
   </ez-page-content>
</ez-page>
```

Layout choice:
- List → `blueprint/patterns/list-page` (filters above, table in `<ez-card flush>`).
- Long detail → `blueprint/patterns/detail-page` (`ez-page-sections` + sections, TOC on the right, cards with `toc-id`).
- Edit/create → `blueprint/patterns/edit-form` (`ez-layout` 8/4, right column `first-below-md`, buttons in the summary card `#footer`).

Do not use `ez-app-shell` in a prototype: the viewer adds the app chrome from `meta.json` (`"chrome": "app"`).

If a needed component doesn't exist, **propose** it in the version, never as raw HTML in `index.vue`:
- `vNNN/components/EzBtnSubmitFolder.vue`, first line `<!-- @proposal domain folder: why it exists -->` (`@proposal primitive: …` only as a last resort).
- Name: `ez-{primitive}-{intention}` (`ez-btn-submit-folder`) or `ez-{object}-{thing}` (`ez-signer-list`).
- A domain proposal only assembles `ez-` components: no colors, borders, shadows, radius (CSS or utilities). Layout (`flex`, `gap`) is fine.
- Import it in `index.vue`: `import EzBtnSubmitFolder from './components/EzBtnSubmitFolder.vue'`.
- Mention it in `notes.md`. Promotion into `blueprint/ez/` is a human decision (`pnpm proto promote`).

A bug in a primitive or a missing method on a mock: never fix `blueprint/` yourself. Work around it in the version if needed and write it in `notes.md` under « Signalements »: `Bug primitive: …`, `Bug helper: …`, `Mock manquant: …`, `Composant manquant: …`. A bug comes with the fix you suggest (file, what to change). `proto check` warns when `blueprint/` has uncommitted changes.

Business data: `blueprint/mocks/API.md` lists every object, property and method (generated). Read it instead of `blueprint/mocks/*.ts`.
